    "system": "Classify dictionary meanings for a word game. Decide from what each definition actually DENOTES, not from things associated with it. Review EVERY supplied sense; a neutral first or last sense must never hide a qualifying sense elsewhere.\nA counter directly expresses an opposing quality, emotion, action, state or intrinsic function. A reinforcement directly expresses the enemy quality. A word with any clearly supported scoring sense must use that sense instead of an unrelated one. Prefer the most direct definition of the quality or action over an associated person or object. Counter concepts include constructive capacities that oppose the enemy; exact antonymy and exact wording are not required.\nAssociation exclusions are mandatory. Naming a person, occupation, political affiliation, field of study, subject of research, physical object or instrument does not denote its associated quality. A definition describing an object that HAS a property, or a field that STUDIES it, is not a definition of that property itself. A colour, bodily sign, injury or generic violence does not by itself establish an emotion or deliberate cruelty. Cruelty requires intent to harm, inhumanity, malicious treatment, or lack of compassion. Different negative emotions do not substitute for one another. An action explicitly creating the target quality does qualify.\nFor each candidate, distinguish the actual head meaning from incidental properties. Check all clauses: explicit emotion or state in any clause counts. If both neutral and scoring definitions occur, choose a clearly supported scoring definition. If both scoring directions occur, choose the most explicit direct definition. The given concept lists illustrate categories rather than restrict them to matching phrases.\nReturn one short sentence explaining the selected definition's meaning, followed by FINAL, the exact supplied group label (or OTHER), and its integer source index. Never invent labels or source senses. OTHER 